P2-WINDOWS W7 — page:driving/TripPlanner — WinUI 3 / Fluent parity port
========================================================================
Web source : web/src/features/driving/pages/TripPlannerPage.tsx (route /trip-planner)
Output     : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/TripPlannerPage/
             (repo convention = C#-markup feature-views, not Features/*.xaml; see sibling
              done pages QuickStatsPage / SmartChargePage / TeslaChargingSessionsPage. The
              generated prompt's path apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Driving does not exist in-repo.)
Nav        : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs —
             PageFactory.Register("TripPlanner", static () => new FeatureViews.Driving.TripPlannerPage())
             (RouteTable already maps Page("TripPlanner","trip-planner",TripsDriving,…) — no route entry added)
Strings    : apps/windows/Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw already carry 28 of the 30 translation.tripPlanner.* /
             common.free keys (catalog-generated). The two keys the web i18n itself never defines
             (tripPlanner.disclaimer, tripPlanner.notFeasible — the web uses an inline t() English fallback)
             resolve through ILocalizer's English-fallback path, the same precedent the sibling AddressInput /
             TripPlannerMap surfaces follow. Every visible literal is sourced by key; none hardcoded.

Files:
  feature-views/TripPlannerPage/TripPlannerPage.Model.cs      (parsers + projection + registration + diagnostics + ports + Noop/Empty)
  feature-views/TripPlannerPage/TripPlannerPage.Source.cs     (generated C# client mutation adapters: PlanTripClient + SendToCarClient)
  feature-views/TripPlannerPage/TripPlannerPage.ViewModel.cs  (INotifyPropertyChanged mutation holder + form state + units/currency)
  feature-views/TripPlannerPage/TripPlannerPage.cs            (WinUI 3 UserControl, Fluent + design tokens)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/TripPlannerPageTests.cs    (21 headless tests)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj              (link the 3 UI-free files; the WinUI view is build-only)

Data sources (P1/S8 INotifyPropertyChanged VM → generated C# client, web hook names kept at the C# call sites):
  usePlanTrip      -> PlanTripClient.PlanAsync, ApiRequest("post_api_v1_trip_planner_plan", Body) — POST /trip-planner/plan
  handleSendToCar  -> SendToCarClient.SendNavigationAsync, ApiRequest("post_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_command",
                      PathParams[vehicleID], Body{ command:"navigation_request", params:{ lat, lon } }) — POST /vehicles/{id}/command
  useSelectedVehicle -> IWidgetVehicleSource.GetPrimaryAsync (vehicle id + battery_level)
Reused W3 component surfaces (driving): AddressInput (origin/destination), TripPlannerMap (map), SOCRouteChart (SOC chart),
  TripLegList (route breakdown) — bound from the parsed TripPlanSnapshot the VM owns.
Units (P1/S5): SI read from the API; converted only at the display boundary in TripPlannerProjection via
  UnitFormatters.FormatDistance/FormatEnergy + ScalarFormatters.FormatCurrency + the composite hours/minutes duration
  (no non-SI stored/computed).
Live data: none (web page uses a TanStack-Query mutation, no useLiveX/SSE), so no SSE subscription / staleness chip (ADR-013 n/a).

